  "answer_text": "You can download the latest version of Python from the **official Python website**. Here are the details:\n\n### \ud83d\udd17 Download Link: **[https://www.python.org/downloads/](https://www.python.org/downloads/)**\n\nThe latest stable release is **Python 3.14.5**, and Python source code and installers are available for download for all versions.\n\nPython 3.14.5 was released on **May 10, 2026**.\n\n---\n\n### Key highlights of Python 3.14:\n- Free-threaded Python is officially supported, and the evaluation of annotations is now deferred, improving the semantics of using annotations.\n- Template string literals (t-strings) for custom string processing, using the familiar syntax of f-strings.\n- A new module `compression.zstd` providing support for the Zstandard compression algorithm.\n- Syntax highlighting in PyREPL, and support for color in `unittest`, `argparse`, `json`, and `calendar` CLIs.\n\n---\n\n### Platform-specific downloads:\n- **Windows:** The installer for Windows is being replaced by a new install manager, which can be installed from the Windows Store or from its download page. You can visit [python.org/downloads/windows/](https://www.python.org/downloads/windows/) for more details.\n- **macOS:** Available at [python.org/downloads/macos/](https://www.python.org/downloads/macos/)\n- **Linux/Unix:** For most Unix systems, you must download and compile the source code. The same source code archive can also be used to build the Windows and Mac versions.\n\nAlways make sure to download Python from the **official python.org website** to ensure you're getting a safe and legitimate copy.",
